{
  "id": "double-simultaneous-stimulation",
  "term": "double-simultaneous stimulation",
  "definition": "Double-simultaneous stimulation is the presentation of two sensory stimuli at the same time, typically one on each side of the body or space, to examine whether a person notices both together. In patients with unilateral brain damage, it can reveal extinction, where the stimulus on the side opposite the lesion is missed when both are given simultaneously.",
